  "id": "Compound::DB01380 - Gene::2908",
  "verbalization": "Cortisone Acetate is linked to Nr3c1 through a shared classification in the Corticosteroid Hormone Receptor Agonists category, which includes compounds like Desonide, Prednicarbate, and Desoximetasone. These compounds all bind to Nr3c1, suggesting a common mechanism of action involving the nuclear receptor Nr3c1. The lowest common ancestors of Cortisone Acetate and these compounds point to the broader category of Therapeutic Glucocorticoid and Corticosteroid Hormone, reinforcing the idea that Cortisone Acetate acts through a glucocorticoid receptor pathway. The consistent binding of these compounds to Nr3c1 implies that Cortisone Acetate may exert its effects by activating Nr3c1, potentially through a shared receptor mechanism. The evidence suggests a direct interaction between Cortisone Acetate and Nr3c1, supported by the inclusion of these compounds in the same class and their binding to the same receptor.",
